  "status_text": "A small drop budget gives a consistent label for any two groups joined by every possible line. Lean checked this for graph answers that can only stay put or fall as the selection grows. An answer must say one if all selected dots are joined to its dot, and zero if its dot is selected. If at most k successive drops are possible, give each ordered pair of such nonempty groups a sign and a number from 1 to 2k minus 3. Swapping the groups flips the sign at the same number. Enlarging both groups keeps or raises the number and preserves the sign at equal numbers (L-lib-1267).",
